course: dictionary
lesson: 6262
title: Molten: melted by heat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Igneous rocks form when molten rock cools and hardens.» Molten means melted by great heat. The clues are "cools and hardens": rock that was melted and very hot goes cold and solid again. So molten must mean melted, the opposite of hard.
explain: Molten rock is called magma while it is still under the ground. When it comes out of a volcano, it is called lava. The word molten describes both, because both are melted by great heat.
explain: The same word works in other places. In design and technology, molten metal is poured into moulds. In cooking, a molten chocolate cake is soft and runny in the middle. To check your meaning, swap "melted by great heat" into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Molten means melted by great heat.
fact: Molten is used about metal, rock or glass, as in molten lava and molten metal.
fact: Molten rock under the ground is magma. When it comes out of a volcano, it is lava.
fact: In cooking, a molten chocolate cake is soft and runny in the middle.
fact: «Igneous rocks» are "fire rocks": they form when molten rock cools and hardens.
exercise: «Igneous rocks form when molten rock cools and hardens.» What does molten mean? | Painted bright red | Cold and hard as stone | Covered in snow | *Melted by great heat
exercise: In design and technology, molten metal is poured into moulds. What is the metal like when it is poured? | Dry like sand | Frozen into ice | Cold and bendy like rubber | *Melted and very hot
exercise: Which word means melted rock that is still under the ground? | Gravel | *Magma | Lava | Pumice
test: «Molten lava» flows out of a volcano. What is the lava like? | *Melted by great heat | Made of wood | Frozen solid like ice | Cold, hard and grey
test: Which sentence uses molten correctly? | The molten bridge was painted blue | The molten snowman stood tall in the cold garden | The molten teacher read a book | *The molten chocolate cake was gooey in the middle
exam: «Igneous rocks form when molten rock cools and hardens.» What happens to molten rock as it cools? | It gets bigger and softer | It floats up into the sky | *It hardens into solid rock | It turns into water and runs away
